## Final answer of writer
I fixed the paging bug in `src/paginate.js`, and `npm test` now passes all 4 tests. Before the fix, 3 of the 4 passed.

The last page's length was computed as `items.length % size`. That is 0 whenever the total is an exact multiple of the page size, so the last page came back empty and its items were dropped. Each page is now just `items.slice(start, start + size)`, and `slice` already stops at the end of the array. That also covers partial last pages and empty input.

The existing test "the last page is full when the total is a multiple of the page size" covers the bug, so I added no new test. The only file changed is `src/paginate.js`, and I left no scratch files.

